From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:27:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ppe: avoid waiting for RTNL during tunnel flow creation

An interface notifier can hold RTNL while flushing the flow-add workqueue.
Do not block that workqueue on RTNL when reading IPIP6 or MAP-E tunnel
parameters. Leave the flow in software when topology is changing, using
the existing pre-publication cleanup for virtual-port and device
references.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
@@ -3683,7 +3683,11 @@
 					       flow->entry.sport,
 		};
 
-		rtnl_lock();
+		/* NETDEV_DOWN holds RTNL while flushing the add workqueue. */
+		if (!rtnl_trylock()) {
+			ret = -EAGAIN;
+			goto err_prelock_ivp;
+		}
 		ret = dev_ip6_tnl_flow_offload(tdev, &key, &tnl_info);
 		rtnl_unlock();
 		if (ret || ipv6_addr_any(&tnl_info.local) ||
